yesterday I participated at the European  Council meeting it was a long and  intense discussion among European  leaders and after which we passed a very  clear message that the European Union  and the Member States will do everything  they can everything necessary to  overcome the coronavirus crisis and we  will do it together in solidarity for  the benefit and protection of our  citizens for that we're taking measures  and measures needed first to limit the  spread of the virus and to provide  urgent assistance to those in need in  the case of the European external  actions this is devoted to our citizens  stranded in third countries to return  home this is an absolute priority we  have more than 400,000 people that want  to go back home  more than 150,000 has already done it  thanks to the air flight that we have  been all the Member States providing  them and more than 2,000 by the European  Union civil assistance use for the  extreme cases where there is no  commercial or chartered flight we have a  task force here in the European Union  external Action Service which is working  around the clock to assist Member States  we are reaching out to third countries  organizing repatriation flights ensuring  landing rights and access to our space  transit access an extension of visas  when needed there is a big problem today  with the access to the air space many  countries are closing it and we have to  ask them to provide an extension of this  closing in order to  allow many more flights to take people  back home we need to limit the spread of  the virus  to promote research so that we can  quickly find a vaccine that would  believe for the benefit of the entire  world here cooperation is much more  needed that competition also you have to  tackle socio-economic consequences this  crisis has created a most urgently to  ensure the provision of medical  equipment the Commission in cooperation  with industry will provide an overview  of stocks production and imports and  take actions to improve the situation we  will also actively pursue its giant  procurement initiative and increase the  initial budget of the strategic European  Union stockpile of medical equipment  especially for intensive care vaccines  and therapeutics in parallel also member  states are supporting each other for  example France Germany and Austria  together are sending 3.5 million masks  and 800,000 protection dresses to Italy  and some member states are taking care  of each other patients to ensure a  hospital capacity for crew solidarity  and support to our partners around the  world is welcomed because solidarity and  international cooperation are at the  heart of a collective success we will  continue working hand-in-hand with our  partners around the world to this end in  Europe we are very grateful for all  genuine offers of help coming from  partner countries from all the world  from the private sector whether in the  provision of maths or other medical  equipment what is important that the  people in need  the necessary help we are promoting  coordination in multilateral fora in the  g7 and in the g20 working with United  Nations and its agencies the Red Cross  we have mobilized 300 million euros to  support partners in combat individuals  around the world channeling this help  through the World Health Organization  for example at the institut pasteur in  that car we are looking in particular at  africa because we want to underline that  we will not forget about our system  continent when addressing this global  pandemic we cannot look only to the  problems in Europe because the problems  in other regions will be sooner or later  also our own problems that why we must  act collectively and the global level we  are playing a role the European Union is  playing a role in doing everything  possible to tackle this crisis and it  consequences is now that we have to  demonstrate that European and global  solidarity really means solidarity can  not be just a 